-no eggs of any of the above

	I can't find anything on whether bats are OK; I suspect they're 
not.  Cockatrices are almost certainly out.  (Like you would want to
eat one anyway...)

	"Beasts of the earth" are OK if they have cloven hooves and chew
the cud.  That means
-no mumak or mastodon
-no dog, wolf, coyote, dingo, or jackal, no cat of any sort
-no mimic, piercer, trapper, or lurker
-no titanothere or baluchitherium
-no horses
-no apes or monkeys

	That leaves us rothes, maybe unicorns...not much else.  It's 
unclear for a whole bunch of things, like centaurs, blobs, jellies, etc.  
